0c2e9b6cd957" :question/math-academy-id "q-160769" :question/problem "What is the value of \n $f(s)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡s\\,i+\\operatorname{cot}⁡s\\,j-\\,k$ at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j-k \\\\  & =1\\,i+1\\,j-k \\\\  & =i+j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of  $f(s)$ at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  is $i+j-k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160769/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26571ec1-e645-5f07-ba4e-75c22558394a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788/selection/ca16e127e4edc86aa0dd86df715a2c3f20a9e3c9708521ba9f45679b0de6fac0" :answer/id #uuid "acea7e88-d8a4-5bca-855a-605cd77f3b02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788/selection/d23151519d79f27e4cebc4ebad9047e36b8453244e6e3d202a56b90321183388" :answer/id #uuid "4468df2c-df9b-51a5-bcbf-0e73d470d544" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788/selection/b95903eade1b06386a44c49a0864d2a1f60e76b5dd90fb33f64198e6f07480b1" :answer/id #uuid "4aeea922-52e6-57a5-8f98-a81aff8cf4fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788/selection/8c00741b9a53ef44debea5378092018f55b03a1263e6867a31123cc747b85a55" :answer/id #uuid "9cb5d7e7-704f-56bb-8714-cb0821775e91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788/selection/0e3bdff03e951f0a388d8b8654d11436ca9d62823f0936e95aee0fe9e94cf8ad" :answer/id #uuid "6ce6e9be-7208-5343-92e6-a95afdd7990e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18da20a7-cf72-5407-90ed-092b7c06752b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160788/selection/d23151519d79f27e4cebc4ebad9047e36b8453244e6e3d202a56b90321183388" :answer-field/choices ["q-160788/selection/ca16e127e4edc86aa0dd86df715a2c3f20a9e3c9708521ba9f45679b0de6fac0" "q-160788/selection/d23151519d79f27e4cebc4ebad9047e36b8453244e6e3d202a56b90321183388" "q-160788/selection/b95903eade1b06386a44c49a0864d2a1f60e76b5dd90fb33f64198e6f07480b1" "q-160788/selection/8c00741b9a53ef44debea5378092018f55b03a1263e6867a31123cc747b85a55" "q-160788/selection/0e3bdff03e951f0a388d8b8654d11436ca9d62823f0936e95aee0fe9e94cf8ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160788" :question/id #uuid "3927b17d-f85e-519c-a173-5cde6f6bc902" :question/math-academy-id "q-160788" :question/problem "What is the value of $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t+1} \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=0?$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t=0$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(0)+1} \\\\ 1-(0)^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=0$ is $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160788/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26571ec1-e645-5f07-ba4e-75c22558394a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160788"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348674/field-1/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "780f5388-cde1-5511-bcf5-517e1e41b178" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348674/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "7a8571cc-5b06-5fa1-a829-0e6af1611490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348674/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "abec40a6-3173-5277-8fe7-ff68dc446a75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348674/field-1/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer-field/choices ["q-348674/field-1/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-348674/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348674" :question/id #uuid "3166e6cc-1fec-5041-af39-f8931c1bf155" :question/math-academy-id "q-348674" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{2}^{t-1},\\,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨{2}^{0},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-348674/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348691/field-1/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" :answer/id #uuid "72e40fdd-b949-585e-87a6-c42741634638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348691/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "51694d70-03c0-5e3f-a9f4-c89722cc078b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348691/field-1/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" :answer-field/choices ["q-348691/field-1/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348691" :question/id #uuid "b1a255b2-db2c-537a-aa22-3b4e70e3f863" :question/math-academy-id "q-348691" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t+3},\\,3\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨\\sqrt{1+3},\\,3\\,{e}^{1-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{4},\\,3\\,{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-348691/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
